  <issue>
  /status table not showing complete information
When using /status table with the RPC telegram bot, it returns existing trades (bought pairs) mixed with open buy orders (pending orders) without any way to differentiate between them.

This is not truthful to the purpose of the function, in the sense that it should convey the difference between these two types, since it also shows Profit, which is false for buy orders that haven't been filled.

This is to log that issue, until a PR I plan to work on is introduced.

We can also discuss how to solve this.

I'm thinking we can add an asterisk (*) next to pairs that aren't owned yet, and to show 0 profit for those. In the sqlite database these can be differentiated by open_order_id.

We can also expand this potential enhancement to show open_bid for those open orders, and open_rate for existing pairs, and current_bid.

Would love to hear your thoughts.

I'm focused at the moment on consistency to polish freqtrade in such areas in small iterations.
  </issue>
  
